/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Working notes and task scratch. Kept out of the history on purpose: it is
# where drafts, measurements and half-finished reasoning go, and none of that
# is the crate.
workspace

# Local agent tooling config. A deploy target for tools that live outside this
# repo, so what lands here is machine state rather than the crate.
.claude

# One worktree per issue lands here. They are checkouts of branches this
# repository already has, so tracking them would commit the same history twice.
.worktrees

# Claude Code also reads CLAUDE.md and CLAUDE.local.md from the directory it
# starts in and every directory above it. The instructions for this repository
# are AGENTS.md, read through .claude/CLAUDE.md above, so either of these
# landing anywhere in the tree is somebody's own and stays out of it. Both the
# anchored and the unanchored form: the anchored one names the repository root
# and stops matching the moment this tree is reached through a link or from a
# worktree, where the root is somewhere else.
/CLAUDE.md
/CLAUDE.local.md
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
